# Build-context exclusions for the Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile copies an explicit list of paths, so most entries here are defence in depth.
# The build-artefact entries are load-bearing: `COPY apps/web apps/web` copies the whole
# directory, and only this file keeps a local `node_modules/`, `build/` or `.svelte-kit/` out.

# --- secrets and appliance identity ---
# Docker ignore patterns are anchored at the context root and do not recurse like .gitignore,
# so each entry has an explicit `**/` twin.
#
# Appliance profile ZIPs and their keys.
secrets/
**/secrets/
secrets/captures/
# Local fleet notes: LAN addresses and appliance MACs.
devices.txt
**/devices.txt
# The API token the server writes at first run, relative to its working directory by default.
kessel.token
**/kessel.token

# --- build artefacts ---
target/
**/target/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
apps/web/build/
apps/web/.svelte-kit/
apps/docs/build/
dist/
scripts/.pylibs/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.profraw
coverage/

# --- repository files no build stage reads ---
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
worktrees/
# Local third-party checkouts and scratch work.
reference/
spike/
# Documentation and project metadata.
docs/
fixtures/
LICENSE
CHANGELOG.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
repository.yaml
release-please-config.json
.DS_Store

# `README.md` is deliberately not excluded: `Cargo.toml` sets `readme = "README.md"`, so the build
# stage copies it.

